{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1347992-growth-and-mega-might-question","id":1347992,"title":"Growth and Mega-Might Question.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-12T13:10:35-08:00","id":1347992,"title":"Growth and Mega-Might Question.","content":"In Trinity Continuum: Aberrant manuscript it states that &quot;Each activated dot of Growth increases the nova\u2019s size Scale by 1 and the nova gains the benefits of 1 dot of Mega-Might as an effect of their new size.&quot;.<br /> <br /> Does this mean that you gain Size equal to Growth +1 and Mega-Might 1, or size equal to Growth+1 and Mega-Might equal to Growth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T13:49:48-08:00","id":1348005,"title":"","content":"If you have Growth 5 and decide to use 2 dots of it, you would add 2 to your Size and 2 to your Mega-Might. If you used all 5 dots, you'd add 5 to your Size and 5 to your Mega-Might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T00:40:02-08:00","id":1348181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1347992-growth-and-mega-might-question?p=1348005#post1348005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have Growth 5 and decide to use 2 dots of it, you would add 2 to your Size and 2 to your Mega-Might. If you used all 5 dots, you'd add 5 to your Size and 5 to your Mega-Might.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, except you don't add 2 to your Mega-Might. You just get two dots of Mega-Might. If you already have Mega-Might, you use either your Growth Mega-Might or base Mega-Might, whichever is better, because they don't stack.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T18:42:20-08:00","id":1349234,"title":"","content":"And if you want to be a super-strong person who becomes a giant, that's when you use techniques to switch up how the dots are arranged, i.e. swapping out the Mega-Might for Growth (which won't make you <i>stronger</i>, but there's enough advantages to size that it could be worthwhile, i.e. reaching sufficient scale to simply no-sell smaller things).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T23:28:34-08:00","id":1349292,"title":"","content":"I honestly don\u2019t see any use for Mega Might as an effect over the already big effect of Size scale. I mean, size scale gives you durability and might scale as a side effect of being big.<br /> <br /> If you pile it up with MMight it is too powerful (also you don\u2019t stack scales), if it don\u2019t give you durability scale to match your size you are too week to fight in that scale. So, as I see, Growth should not give any extra beside the proper size scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T01:05:20-08:00","id":1349298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1347992-growth-and-mega-might-question?p=1349292#post1349292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don\u2019t see any use for Mega Might as an effect over the already big effect of Size scale. I mean, size scale gives you durability and might scale as a side effect of being big.<br /> <br /> If you pile it up with MMight it is too powerful (also you don\u2019t stack scales), if it don\u2019t give you durability scale to match your size you are too week to fight in that scale. So, as I see, Growth should not give any extra beside the proper size scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that saying that there's Mega-Might is probably redundant. Maybe they wanted to make it clear that you could qualify for Mega-Might mega-edges while using Growth? I don't know.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}